From b4700e2ff2586446bf0dca34631e7cb041c2efc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 06:52:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: tiled FA K/V scratch, tiled transposed concat,
 16-wide k-quant A loads, DMA for large BAR writes

- FA coopmat1 prefill with quantized KV: the f16 dequant prepass writes K and V in
  16x16 tiles (K row-major, V transposed), so each fragment load is one contiguous
  512 byte run instead of a 16-row gather (flag bit 64). 10-20% faster FA.
- concat along dim 0 with a transposed src1 (ssm conv state) goes through 32x32
  shared-memory tiles: 781 -> 192 us for the Qwen3.x conv concat.
- mul_mm f16 path: q4_K/q5_K/q6_K threads load 16 values of one sub-block, decoding
  the scales once instead of per 4 (or 2) values. q6_K uses this path on RDNA4
  instead of the int8 MMQ.
- Synchronous writes >= 4 MiB into host-visible VRAM use a staging copy: CPU
  stores across a PCIe x4 BAR ran at ~1 GB/s (130 ms for the 64K-context mask).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FmvwGP4C3tVMNpTvhiju7x
